# kodekloud Cluster Archictecture notes:
High-level overview of cluster architecture

Master node: control-plane components (manage, plan, schedule, monitor nodes)
- node controllers - replication controller, node controller etc.
- etcd - key value store. Stores information of the cluster, database fo the cluster
- scheduler - load containers on worker nodes
- kube-apiserver - responsible for orhestrating all the operations within the cluster

Worker nodes: (host application as containers)
- kubelet - is an agent installed in the worker nodes that listens instructions from the kube-api server and manages containers. 
- containers - docker/containerd
- pods - think of it as "wrapper" for the containers
- kube-proxy service - is responsible to create rules to allow containers (applications) from one node to another to communicate (via services ) with each other in a cluster. 


